            <ArticleTitle>Coronary Dissection Discovered During Ex Vivo Organ Preservation: Avoiding a Fatal Complication.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e383-e384</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0003-4975(17)30845-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.athoracsur.2017.05.087</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes the case of undiagnosed posttraumatic coronary artery dissection in a young multiorgan donor. Ex vivo preservation with the Organ Care System (TransMedics, Inc, Andover, MA) revealed the presence of coronary disease and avoided transplantation of an organ at high risk for failure.</AbstractText>
